# Clarity — optional environment configuration
#
# IMPORTANT: this file is documentation, not a loaded config. Clarity has no
# dotenv dependency and nothing reads a .env file at runtime, so copying this to
# `.env` on its own has no effect. Export the variables in the environment that
# launches the app instead:
#
#   CLARITY_DISABLE_GPU=1 npm run dev
#
# Every variable below is OPTIONAL and none of them is a secret. Clarity holds no
# API keys, no database credentials and no account of any kind: it is a local
# desktop app with no backend, no authentication and no paid services. Copy this
# file only if you want a written record of the switches available to you.


# Disable GPU/hardware acceleration. Set to 1 on machines where the compositor
# causes rendering artefacts or crashes on launch.
# CLARITY_DISABLE_GPU=1

# Override the path to the bundled IEEE OUI registry, used to name Wi-Fi access
# point vendors. Defaults to the copy shipped in the app resources.
# CLARITY_OUI_PATH=/absolute/path/to/oui.json

# Where to upload crash minidumps. Left unset — the default — the crash reporter
# writes dumps locally and uploads nothing at all. Only set this if you are
# running your own crash collector; it is a plain endpoint URL, not a key, and
# anything you put here is sent from users' machines.
# CLARITY_CRASH_URL=https://crashes.example.com/submit
